[{:db/id "q-8479/selection/baa9c5706dc48ea8c267a4346bec9881ac87ae06f837cc6ff922a4a28c2699a6" :answer/id #uuid "33bd5351-db78-5a1d-94ec-cfeffa31ba3b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5{\\pi }^{2}}{24}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8479/selection/c42f647fc20b0fb30561ace08cd0a922968ea287ed93bdf6f927ff5a6892dd82" :answer/id #uuid "4df24be7-7040-5495-b853-b92e41afb9e9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{85\\pi }{576}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8479/selection/86f78fab2dcbb8ccc674faeb155d1c4ab97abf9d97d47609ecd2ca80aaba99b8" :answer/id #uuid "a7508151-97d1-52bb-bac2-9bad8852abcb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{85{\\pi }^{2}}{24}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8479/selection/d8e385ae08da5fc0b455deade2b65d9e383f125deca409fb0db3a6592d1c26a8" :answer/id #uuid "21693bd1-8502-56ad-a254-0db26b8ff31f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{85{\\pi }^{2}}{576}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8479/selection/fd2259bca62104fc2d9fdce2a6004c1d372a6ff4a6a4a0e3e3613fbc8e65f276" :answer/id #uuid "9681b628-9399-5a9f-8b7f-8b6a234949fc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{17{\\pi }^{2}}{576}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8479/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e2a71cf1-f245-5ce1-94e5-a1187e76e035" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-8479/selection/d8e385ae08da5fc0b455deade2b65d9e383f125deca409fb0db3a6592d1c26a8" :answer-field/choices ["q-8479/selection/baa9c5706dc48ea8c267a4346bec9881ac87ae06f837cc6ff922a4a28c2699a6" "q-8479/selection/c42f647fc20b0fb30561ace08cd0a922968ea287ed93bdf6f927ff5a6892dd82" "q-8479/selection/86f78fab2dcbb8ccc674faeb155d1c4ab97abf9d97d47609ecd2ca80aaba99b8" "q-8479/selection/d8e385ae08da5fc0b455deade2b65d9e383f125deca409fb0db3a6592d1c26a8" "q-8479/selection/fd2259bca62104fc2d9fdce2a6004c1d372a6ff4a6a4a0e3e3613fbc8e65f276"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-8479" :question/id #uuid "c4570ce6-8681-560b-93a0-ff873c068a50" :question/math-academy-id "q-8479" :question/problem "Consider the equation $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi .$ Given that the exact solutions ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3}$ and ${x}_{4}$ are written in ascending order, what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "We will find the general solution to the equation, and then generate all of the solutions in the required domain.\n\nThe general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-\\frac{\\pi }{4} & =\\frac{\\pi }{6}+n\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the equation above for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\frac{\\pi }{6}+n\\pi  \\\\ 2x & =\\frac{5\\pi }{12}+n\\pi  \\\\ x & =\\frac{n\\pi }{2}+\\frac{5\\pi }{24}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe set $n=0,\\pm 1,\\pm 2,…,$ until we have generated all solutions in the domain $0\\le x<2\\pi .$\n\n- Setting $n=0$ gives $x=\\frac{5\\pi }{24}$\n\n- Setting $n=1$ gives $x=\\frac{17\\pi }{24}$\n\n- Setting $n=2$ gives $x=\\frac{29\\pi }{24}$\n\n- Setting $n=3$ gives $x=\\frac{41\\pi }{24}$\n\nAll other values of $n$ generate solutions outside the domain $0\\le x<2\\pi .$ So, the solutions ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3},{x}_{4}$ (written in ascending order) are\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{5\\pi }{24},\\frac{17\\pi }{24},\\frac{29\\pi }{24},\\frac{41\\pi }{24}.\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${x}_{1}=\\frac{5\\pi }{24}$ and ${x}_{2}=\\frac{17\\pi }{24},$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=\\frac{5\\pi }{24}\\cdot \\frac{17\\pi }{24}=\\frac{85{\\pi }^{2}}{576}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-8479/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f3bd5e5c-b8d1-53e5-9968-8bef8faceb4b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-8479"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-8557/selection/e61895e6e81064ea02189d56b088e7ae8cb398470ba2fb826a859863d679bb27" :answer/id #uuid "498bf143-4564-53e5-85eb-b32de2c5b41a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{13{\\pi }^{2}}{24}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8557/selection/ee780c54c894678ffde7f4768068beaa6701e4d0bbd5f57a0cf165232376b284" :answer/id #uuid "da4af912-afaa-51c5-8bb6-1232477cf03b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{13\\pi }{24}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8557/selection/2110c0b8c4b640c118be70e8ea12974a4901aebcc05cf5c94f27a6fa8292d60a" :answer/id #uuid "3d612ae0-6b0e-5a1f-af24-a1113e212283" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{13\\pi }{576}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8557/selection/9afb65ea0b7859138a305e14d91c0058a92195e3e4ddbc019f5106e9dcf4394f" :answer/id #uuid "d56d1bc8-98f4-5684-962d-6fff8e046866" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{13{\\pi }^{2}}{576}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8557/selection/771a0dae111578e289cbc71683beadc36fa8ddd6c0659aef475cf54daf4b9862" :answer/id #uuid "690e7bf6-e386-59a3-825b-a2c7d3b899c5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{13{\\pi }^{2}}{576}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8557/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "497c3159-d911-5616-9754-02dbc7702710" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-8557/selection/9afb65ea0b7859138a305e14d91c0058a92195e3e4ddbc019f5106e9dcf4394f" :answer-field/choices ["q-8557/selection/e61895e6e81064ea02189d56b088e7ae8cb398470ba2fb826a859863d679bb27" "q-8557/selection/ee780c54c894678ffde7f4768068beaa6701e4d0bbd5f57a0cf165232376b284" "q-8557/selection/2110c0b8c4b640c118be70e8ea12974a4901aebcc05cf5c94f27a6fa8292d60a" "q-8557/selection/9afb65ea0b7859138a305e14d91c0058a92195e3e4ddbc019f5106e9dcf4394f" "q-8557/selection/771a0dae111578e289cbc71683beadc36fa8ddd6c0659aef475cf54daf4b9862"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-8557" :question/id #uuid "3eb110db-f4a7-568d-994f-26f7cca1ce4e" :question/math-academy-id "q-8557" :question/problem "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the exact solutions to the equation $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x-\\frac{11\\pi }{6})=1$ for $0\\le x<\\pi ,$ what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "We will find the general solution to the equation, and then generate all of the solutions in the required domain.\n\nThe general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-\\frac{11\\pi }{6} & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}+n\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the equation above for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & =\\frac{11\\pi }{6}+\\frac{\\pi }{4}+n\\pi  \\\\ 2x & =\\frac{25\\pi }{12}+n\\pi  \\\\ x & =\\frac{25\\pi }{24}+\\frac{n\\pi }{2} \\\\ x & =\\frac{(12n+25)\\pi }{24}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe set $n=0,\\pm 1,\\pm 2,…,$ until we have generated all solutions in the domain $0\\le x<\\pi .$\n\n- Setting $n=-2$ gives $x=\\frac{\\pi }{24}$\n\n- Setting $n=-1$ gives $x=\\frac{13\\pi }{24}$\n\nAll other values of $n$ generate solutions outside the domain $0\\le x<\\pi .$ So, the solutions are $x=\\frac{\\pi }{24},\\frac{13\\pi }{24}.$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{24}\\cdot \\frac{13\\pi }{24}=\\frac{13{\\pi }^{2}}{576}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-8557/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9eb12a99-5169-52f7-8830-5de0d2d854f6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-8557"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-82373/selection/bdf7fb4b96dfe4af8e5e9bd95d58fb5b2fe30aabf848faa9f7bd6b5c4a1b6fcf" :answer/id #uuid "f01c2a25-6356-5cf6-8c46-114c3db75ddc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\,005" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82373/selection/d06aa95afa14a41199599988018a5e5cc079356500bc85c18ccd100edcb200dd" :answer/id #uuid "d5f61731-1626-5143-9f3b-1411cc5557f8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\,526" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82373/selection/8cbd6ff72a7a6679acadbd1861b5ab09f31e328ab9a7009aa55d60e757ada7c1" :answer/id #uuid "803984a4-031c-5a40-820c-8fa963cf49f3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\,265" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82373/selection/b66aea22d008baef1aded790f17772ce96ce6b59686abf6b848c11cc8c47c5bd" :answer/id #uuid "fb1150d8-fbf5-54ac-8f7c-5d00aa29736a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6\\,750" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82373/selection/f8d580d0cc40a393866adc60422fb5850b02f4ff188beedc0227a3e89347ed13" :answer/id #uuid "bf8d4ab6-6044-5b97-af0d-ad2e27cff690" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6\\,075" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-82373/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5157c32d-d421-56a1-994d-8a3d81fedcc9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-82373/selection/f8d580d0cc40a393866adc60422fb5850b02f4ff188beedc0227a3e89347ed13" :answer-field/choices ["q-82373/selection/bdf7fb4b96dfe4af8e5e9bd95d58fb5b2fe30aabf848faa9f7bd6b5c4a1b6fcf" "q-82373/selection/d06aa95afa14a41199599988018a5e5cc079356500bc85c18ccd100edcb200dd" "q-82373/selection/8cbd6ff72a7a6679acadbd1861b5ab09f31e328ab9a7009aa55d60e757ada7c1" "q-82373/selection/b66aea22d008baef1aded790f17772ce96ce6b59686abf6b848c11cc8c47c5bd" "q-82373/selection/f8d580d0cc40a393866adc60422fb5850b02f4ff188beedc0227a3e89347ed13"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-82373" :question/id #uuid "ca5d3a4d-d32a-5591-b61b-0726227bd885" :question/math-academy-id "q-82373" :question/problem "Consider the equation $\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x-{45}^{∘})-\\sqrt{3}=0$ for ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}.$ If the exact solutions ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3}$ and ${x}_{4}$ are written in ascending order, what is the numerical value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x-{45}^{∘})-\\sqrt{3} & =0 \\\\ \\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x-{45}^{∘}) & =\\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x-{45}^{∘}) & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x-{45}^{∘}) & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will find the general solution to the equation, and then generate all of the solutions in the required domain.\n\nThe general solution to our equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-{45}^{∘} & ={45}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving our equation for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & ={45}^{∘}+{45}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘} \\\\ 2x & ={90}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={45}^{∘}+n\\cdot {90}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe set $n=0,\\pm 1,\\pm 2,…,$ until we have generated all solutions in the domain ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}.$\n\n- Setting $n=0$ gives $x={45}^{∘}$\n\n- Setting $n=1$ gives $x={135}^{∘}$\n\n- Setting $n=2$ gives $x={225}^{∘}$\n\n- Setting $n=3$ gives $x={315}^{∘}$\n\nAll other values of $n$ generate solutions outside the domain ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}.$ So, the solutions ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3}$ and ${x}_{4}$ (written in ascending order) are\n\n$$\nx={45}^{∘},{135}^{∘},{225}^{∘},{315}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the numerical value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$ is $45\\cdot 135=6\\,075.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-82373/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f3bd5e5c-b8d1-53e5-9968-8bef8faceb4b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-82373"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-328350/field-1/51ce6fbd5c5ce79c5100a77800bd4350632d7271f3ee46e928b7f10cd9572e1c" :answer/id #uuid "a9afd5b5-4ca7-5dc7-831d-30f699365815" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{12}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-328350/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "190cb89e-aebf-5c8e-b23b-575fc6dd86fa" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-328350/field-1/51ce6fbd5c5ce79c5100a77800bd435063